/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is deliberately committed. This crate is not consumed as a Rust library; it is a
# cdylib compiled into a binary that ships inside the NuGet package, and CI rebuilds those binaries
# and only proposes them when the bytes change. An unpinned dependency graph would make that
# comparison meaningless, and `cargo build --locked` cannot create a lockfile it does not find.
pkg/
wasm-pack.log
node_modules
/build/*/**
!/build/*/package.json
.env
.Net/OPAQUE.Net/.vs
.Net/OPAQUE.Net/obj
.Net/OPAQUE.Net/bin
.Net/Test/obj
bin
target